OPERATING SYSTEMS SUITE (OSSim)
Publicly Available, Source-Protected Educational Software Distribution
Interactive Pedagogical Simulation Suite • Architecture Laboratory

Author, Creator & Designer: Sivraj P.
Co-Developed & Engineered with: Antigravity (Google DeepMind)
Curricular Foundation: The syllabus of 23ELC211 Operating Systems, B.Tech.
Electrical and Computer Engineering, Department of Electrical and Electronics
Engineering, Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham was used as the basic course to set
the structure.

(C) Copyright Sivraj P. All rights reserved.

SOFTWARE CLASSIFICATION:
OSSim is a publicly available, source-protected educational software distribution.
Access to the public repository and distribution bundle is provided free of charge
for higher-education teaching, academic study, and educational research. It is
not open source; proprietary core implementation protections remain in effect.

PERMITTED USES & PERMISSIONS:
1. Educational & Classroom Use: Faculty, instructors, and teaching assistants are
   explicitly authorized to distribute unmodified standalone distribution copies
   (zip archives, offline bundles) directly to enrolled students for academic
   coursework and laboratory assignments.
2. Institutional Mirroring: Colleges, universities, and accredited educational
   institutions are explicitly granted permission to host unmodified internal mirror
   copies on secure campus intranets, local servers, or institutional Learning
   Management Systems (Canvas, Moodle, Blackboard) for enrolled student access.
3. Academic Research & Publications: Researchers, educators, and students are
   explicitly permitted to reproduce screenshots, experiment logs, Gantt charts,
   and simulation metrics generated by OSSim in academic papers, theses, textbooks,
   and conference presentations, subject to standard scholarly attribution.
4. Citation Requirement: Any publication, research paper, course syllabus, or
   academic presentation referencing or using OSSim must cite:
   "OSSim: Operating Systems Simulation Suite, Designed by Sivraj P. (2026)."

RESTRICTIONS & PROTECTIONS:
1. Reverse Engineering & Extraction Prohibited: The compiled runtime distribution
   bundle and client-side code protections must remain intact. Unauthorized
   decompilation, reverse engineering, decryption, disassembly, unauthorized
   extraction of proprietary visualizer/solver modules, or creation of derivative
   forks without express prior written permission of Sivraj P. is strictly
   prohibited under the Indian Copyright Act, 1957 and applicable international
   copyright conventions.
2. Commercial Use Prohibited: Commercial sale, paid licensing, commercial training
   bundling, or incorporating OSSim into paid commercial products without explicit
   written licensing agreement is strictly prohibited.
